        "expression": "jython:import re\nThis task requires additional data not provided, specifically the PPP loan amounts for each city. Here's an example of how you could structure your code once you have that data:\n\n\nloans = {\n    'Honolulu': 1000000,\n    'Holualoa': 200000,\n    'Lihue': 50000,\n\n}\n\ncities_with_highest_loans = loans.sort_values(reverse=True).head(3)\nprint(\"Cities with the highest amount of PPP loans:\")\nfor city, loan in cities_with_highest_loans.items():\n    print(\"%s\" % ({city}: ${loan}))\n\n\nThis code sorts the loans dictionary by value (the loan amounts) in descending order and prints the top 3 cities with their corresponding loan amounts. Adjust the number of cities to be printed by changing the `head()` function argument.\nreturn value",
